      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="684906413">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="54.144867" lon="-113.637833" />
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="985002">Strider&#39;s Ride</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP735	 Clyde&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We were making our way south after the long trek up to Slave Lake today and as it happens, there was one last piece of capping business to attend to. For no other reason than pure happenstance, this will probably be my last ever cap find [loggable find at least]. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks Brian for maintaining and keeping this excellent moving cache going strong over the years!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="680988707">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-24T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1565005">Takin it Easy</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP735 Clyde 47 Ave

Posted: N54° 08.690 W113° 38.269

GPSr: N54° 08.692 W113° 38.270&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I headed north from Rundle Park and by the time I got to Clyde, the rain/snow mix had subsided.  I have been to Clyde before and that was for a cap as well.  I had not ventured into town though.  I got to GZ,  parked by the homes and walked over to GZ.  The area had 3&quot; of wet snow cover.  I checked the context photo, pulled out the shovel and started clearing snow.  I had cleared a 15' by 10' section before I found the cap depression pretty close to the post.  I had totally misread the provided photo's perspective.  Doh! Thankfully it was near freezing today and this hole was nice and dry once the snow was removed.  I spent 20 minutes clearing snow here, but I still had 10 minutes of wiggle room, so I continued on with my original plan and headed west to Barrhead.  Thanks for the cap OFTH!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="641102878">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="54.144833" lon="-113.637817" />
          <groundspeak:date>2016-10-01T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="321730">Sleepy_hollow</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP735 - Clyde 47 Ave&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I got a later start today from Edmonton after wrapping things up at the Shaw Conference Centre. Getting out of the core in Edmonton is simply not nice - construction is really everywhere! Once on the highway I made good time and quickly found the BGL cap and got it ready for the money shot - nice spot on a sunny day - thanks OFTH for setting it up!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="640462330">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-09-27T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="664594">Sears Tower</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP735 - Clyde 47 Ave&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;OK, so it is in the middle of no where, but there weren't any other closer.  TFTH&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
